From f661773527b1f881f5d4cd4b384cc6089f080af5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:44:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Serve the frames as JSON lines for other renderers; place and
 park a critter

critterd --stream [PATH] publishes the frame slot on a second Unix socket (30 Hz by default, nothing
serialised while nobody listens), so a renderer that is not Rust can draw the sim: the Caelestia shell uses
it on Hyprland, where there is no overlay of our own yet. The frame types derive serde, and the wire format
is critter_core::stream.

ControlRequest::Place puts the critter somewhere the world does not know (a drawer of the shell), on the
front lane, flying off with a velocity: it forgets its intent and flies the throw ballistically until it
stands on something. Park hides and pauses it. critterctl gets place and park.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
