+### Drawing them from another program
+
+`critterd --stream` serves the frames as JSON lines on a Unix socket (`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/desktop-critters-frames.sock`,
+or the path you give it), about 30 a second: `{"t": 12.3, "frame": {"outputs": [...], "critters": [...], "decals": [...]}}`.
+A critter has its `body` rect (the feet are its bottom centre), its `pose` (`kind`, `facing`, `phase`, `squash`,
+`tilt`...), the `layer` and the window rects in front of it (`occluders`, not to be painted inside). That is
+everything a renderer needs, so it works on Hyprland, where there is no overlay of our own yet: the
+Caelestia shell draws its dashboard cat that way. `critterctl place X Y --vx --vy` throws the critter in from
+somewhere the world does not know, and `critterctl park` hides and pauses it.
+
